        {"@type":"Question","name":"What spaces go inside French quotation marks?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A nonbreaking space separates the text from « and ». A narrow nonbreaking space gives a refined result: « exemple ». A normal nonbreaking space is a sound fallback."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Where does the period go with French quotation marks?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Punctuation belonging to the quoted speech stays inside: « Pourquoi ? ». Sentence punctuation follows the closing mark when the quoted words are integrated into the sentence."}},
